course: dictionary
lesson: 14078
title: Meanly: unkind, stingy or shabby
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Meanly is an adverb. It tells you how someone does something, and most often it means in an unkind or nasty way. «She laughed meanly when Tom tripped over his bag.» Nobody laughs kindly at a friend who has fallen, so the word shows that the laugh was cruel.
explain: Meanly can also mean stingy, which means not willing to share or spend. «He meanly kept the last biscuit and would not share even a crumb.» The clue is would not share, so meanly tells you he was not generous.
explain: Meanly can also mean poorly or shabbily, as in «The old tent was meanly patched with bits of plastic.» Here the word describes how something looks or is made, not how someone behaves. Look at the words around meanly to decide which meaning fits.
fact: Meanly means in an unkind or nasty way.
fact: Meanly can mean stingy, not willing to share or spend.
fact: Meanly can mean poorly or shabbily, as in «meanly dressed».
fact: Meanly is an adverb, so it tells you how an action is done.
fact: To check your meaning, swap in a simpler word: if «unkindly» or «stingily» fits the sentence, you have found the right meaning.
exercise: «The boys meanly hid Sam's bag behind the bins.» What does meanly mean here? | In a loud way | In a fair and kind way | *In an unkind, nasty way | In a quick way
exercise: «Ms Lee meanly refused to share her sandwich, even with her hungry friend.» What does meanly suggest? | Cheerful and happy | *Stingy, not willing to share | Sleepy and slow | Generous and kind
exercise: Find and copy the adverb that tells how she laughed: «She laughed meanly.» | laughed meanly | *meanly | she | laughed
test: «He spoke meanly to his little sister and made her cry.» What does meanly mean? | *In an unkind way | In a happy way | In a very quiet way | In a shy way
test: «The old tent was meanly patched with bits of plastic.» In this sentence, meanly means | Kindly and generously | Quickly | *Poorly, shabbily | Very bravely
exam: Which sentence uses meanly to mean stingy? | The dog meanly barked at the postman | *He meanly kept the last biscuit to himself | The team meanly cheered for their captain | She meanly gave her friend a flower
